<h1 data-scramble-in>sp3ctr-zone</h1>
<p class="lede">░▒▓ a signal from the underground ▓▒░</p>

<p class="prompt">the corporate web runs on the same trade in every direction:
  your attention metered, your behavior profiled, your data warehoused for
  whoever's buying this quarter. that's not a bug in the business model —
  it is the business model, and no "we take your privacy seriously" banner
  changes what the servers are actually doing.</p>
<p class="prompt">governments watch too, and not primarily to protect you.
  surveillance capacity built for one target gets pointed at another the
  moment it's convenient — journalists, organizers, whistleblowers, anyone
  asking questions somebody powerful would rather not answer. the
  infrastructure doesn't discriminate. history isn't short on "temporary"
  programs that never once got smaller.</p>
<p class="prompt">so: trust but verify. don't believe a claim because it
  sounds right, and don't believe mine either — view source, read the
  code, check it yourself. encrypt what actually matters, keep backups,
  look out for the people around you. they can't stop us all, but only if
  we act like it.</p>

